"If enabled, the WebSocket opening handshake headers are enhanced with the 'Sec-WebSocket-Protocol' sub-protocol that match format 'quarkus-http-upgrade++#++header-name++#++header-value'. If the WebSocket client interface does not support setting headers to the WebSocket opening handshake, this is a way how to set authorization header required to authenticate user. The 'quarkus-http-upgrade' sub-protocol is removed and server selects from the sub-protocol one that is supported (don't forget to configure the 'quarkus.websockets-next.server.supported-subprotocols' property). *IMPORTANT: We strongly recommend to only enable this feature if the HTTP connection is encrypted via TLS, CORS origin check is enabled and custom WebSocket ticket system is in place. Please see the Quarkus WebSockets Next reference for more information.*\n"
